{
  "_about": "Contract fixture of Modus B (plan E2.3-E2.6, WP62). One truth for backend tests (FakeLLMClient scripts), frontend tests (fake API) and e2e (model stub). Cases follow design/e2 (screen codes M1-M16) but use the real sample data: the E1 reference question answers 10 of 137 schools (e2e/fixtures/reference-question.json; gemeinden_steuern is imported by the test). 'answer' is what the model returns (D7), serialised to JSON as the completion text; 'raw' replaces it where the model's text is not that JSON. 'expect' is what the application must make of it: 'status' the record's status once the model has answered (an auto answer is 'approved' and the client executes it, D2), or 'http' and 'error_code' where the request is refused before any model call and no record is written. 'setup' names state a test arranges first. Numbers marked null are pinned by the WP that first runs them.",
  "version": 1,
  "levels": [
    {
      "name": "Assistenz",
      "selectable": true,
      "matrix": {
